{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>You shall not bow down to their gods and you shall not serve them.</b> The Torah warns concerning idolatry in several places. And even though the verses are redundant in it, one should not be troubled by that, for because of the severity that is in it — for whoever acknowledges it denies the entire Torah (Chullin 5a) — it warns and goes back and warns, as one who says to his servant: remember constantly, and do not forget the great principle that I have commanded you, upon which everything depends. And it is possible that it warns in the Ten Commandments that he shall not make for himself idolatry and shall not serve it, and now it warns concerning idolatry that they will find already made and worshipped by the nations in the land, that they shall not serve it at all, but rather uproot it from the land." "<b>And you shall not do according to their deeds.</b> It is possible that this is a warning against the ways of the Amorites that the Sages enumerated (Shabbat 67a), just as it warns in another place: \"and you shall not walk in their statutes\" (Leviticus 18:3), and they said (in the Sifra there): these are the ways of the Amorites that the Sages enumerated. And the more plausible interpretation is that it warns concerning idolatry, that one may not serve it in its manner even through an act of worship that is not in a manner of honor, as they expounded (Sanhedrin 61a) on the verse \"How do these nations serve their gods? I will do so as well\" (Deuteronomy 12:30). And the reason is that it said \"you shall not bow down to their gods and you shall not serve them,\" and worship is the honor that a slave performs for his master; and it went back and said that even a matter that is not worship but rather degradation, such as Peor — where one exposes himself before Peor — and throwing a stone at Mercurius, if they practiced it to do thus for them, you shall not do it for them at all. And they said (Sanhedrin 64a): even though he intends to degrade Peor, and even though he intends to stone Mercurius."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:15:25.192777450Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}